3
00:22:36,923 --> 00:22:42,923
During the chaotic final weeks of the Vietnam War, the North Vietnamese Army closes in on
Saigon as the panicked South Vietnamese people desperately attempt to escape.

4
00:30:09,230 --> 00:30:15,230
On the ground, American soldiers and diplomats confront a moral quandary:
whether to obey White House orders to evacuate only U.S.

5
00:37:41,538 --> 00:37:47,538
Last Days in Vietnam is a 2014 American documentary film
written, produced and directed by Rory Kennedy.

6
00:45:13,846 --> 00:45:19,846
The film had its world premiere at 2014 Sundance
Film Festival on January 17, 2014.

7
00:52:46,153 --> 00:52:52,153
After its premiere at Sundance Film Festival, American Experience Films acquired the
distribution rights of the film, in association with PBS Distribution for DVD releases.

8
01:00:18,461 --> 01:00:24,461
The film had a theatrical release in New York City on September 5, 2014, before
expanding nationwide in the United States during September and early October.

9
01:07:50,769 --> 01:07:56,769
The film was nominated for the Academy Award for Best
Documentary Feature at the 87th Academy Awards.

10
01:15:23,076 --> 01:15:29,076
It also garnered a nomination for Best Documentary
Screenplay from the Writers Guild of America.

11
01:22:55,384 --> 01:23:01,384
It premiered on PBS television on April 28, 2015.

12
01:30:27,692 --> 01:30:33,692
The film explores themes of vietnam war, vietnam, woman
director, vietnamese refugees, fall of saigon.
